# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# The automap and the journal's reader together on Curse of the Azure
# Bonds (#588), the one subset where two seams want the same pixels, as
# Pool of Radiance's subset-map-reader is. curse-quiet's keys, then at
# the party's bar after the innkeeper: Tab puts the map over the roster,
# N opens the log over the whole screen, Return opens entry 31, N turns
# to its second page, E goes back to the log and E closes it. The screen
# the program composes then has the map on it again; Tab takes it away,
# Tab brings it back, and a Right turns the party. On Curse the composer
# and the roster's drawer are overlaid and called through stub entries
# (docs/seams.md §10), which is where this give-back differs from Pool
# of Radiance's. 84 checkpoints, the framebuffer in every one;
# tests/visual/curse-map-back.leg says the same in pixels.
#
# Recorded on the Steam copy with its shipped slots A and B (games/curse-slots), at --speed 386 and --wall none.

about the automap up, the journal's log and an entry read over it, the map
about given back with the screen, and Tab still its key: two seams sharing
about the roster's cells
disk external
journal-store tests/visual/curse-reader-store.txt

